  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda - Clean Cooking Stoves</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The government of Rwanda launched a world-bank sponsored clean-cooking initiative as part of its Biomass Energy Strategy. The objectives were to reduce the percentage of households using firewood for cooking from current 79.9% to 42% in 2024; and to phase out use of charcoal in Urban area. Waybreed is to supply 100.000 clean cooking stoves as part of this strategy. Hereby supporting jobs in Pakistan, where the stoves are sourced from, Rwanda and the Netherlands.</narrative>
  </description>
